add(2013,8,5,'Strict concavity on a fixed-sum polytope rules out odd sizes above one; symmetric pairs give every even size.','Unit semicircle heights with zero horizontal sum',r'Find all positive integers $n$ for which real numbers $-1<x_i<1$ can satisfy $\sum_{i=1}^n x_i=0$ and $\sum_{i=1}^n\sqrt{1-x_i^2}=1$.',r'The answers are $n=1$ and all even $n$. For $n=1$, take $x_1=0$. For even $n$, take half the values equal to $t=\sqrt{1-1/n^2}$ and half equal to $-t$. For an odd $n>1$, consider the concave function $F=\sum\sqrt{1-x_i^2}$ on the compact polytope $-1\le x_i\le1,\sum x_i=0$. A minimum occurs at a vertex, where all but at most one coordinate are $\pm1$ (otherwise two coordinates can be moved oppositely). Since $n$ is odd, the remaining coordinate must be 0, so the minimum is 1. At a point with every coordinate strictly inside the interval and $n>1$, moving two coordinates oppositely in either direction gives strict concavity, so such a point cannot attain the minimum. Thus the required sum is strictly greater than 1.','Algebra',['Inequalities','Concavity','Extremal arguments','Constructions'],source=s)
